WEBVTT

00:00.440 --> 00:02.240
Luke, 24

00:02.240 --> 00:06.180
But on the first day of the week, at early dawn,

00:06.500 --> 00:09.180
they went to the tomb, taking the spices they had prepared.

00:09.720 --> 00:12.380
And they found the stone rolled away from the tomb,

00:12.780 --> 00:16.180
but when they went in they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus.

00:17.140 --> 00:18.980
While they were perplexed about this,

00:19.440 --> 00:22.300
behold, two men stood by them in dazzling apparel.

00:22.960 --> 00:26.160
And as they were frightened and bowed their faces to the ground,

00:26.840 --> 00:27.940
the men said to them,

00:27.940 --> 00:31.100
Why do you seek the living among the dead?

00:31.680 --> 00:33.880
He is not here, but has risen.

00:34.760 --> 00:37.660
Remember how he told you while he was still in Galilee,

00:38.340 --> 00:42.080
that the Son of Man must be delivered into the hands of sinful men

00:42.080 --> 00:45.320
and be crucified, and on the third day rise.

00:46.180 --> 00:47.780
And they remembered his words,

00:47.960 --> 00:51.240
and returning from the tomb they told all these things to the eleven

00:51.240 --> 00:52.460
and to all the rest.

00:53.200 --> 00:56.940
Now it was Mary Magdalene and Joanna and Mary the mother of James

00:56.940 --> 00:57.920
and the other women of the church,

00:57.920 --> 01:00.340
and the women with them who told these things to the apostles.

01:00.900 --> 01:03.280
But these words seemed to them an idle tale,

01:03.380 --> 01:04.680
and they did not believe them.

01:05.840 --> 01:07.920
But Peter rose and ran to the tomb.

01:08.620 --> 01:11.660
Stooping and looking in, he saw the linen cloths by themselves.

01:12.460 --> 01:15.300
And he went home marveling at what had happened.

01:17.000 --> 01:20.600
That very day two of them were going to a village named Emmaus,

01:20.980 --> 01:22.640
about seven miles from Jerusalem,

01:23.080 --> 01:26.440
and they were talking with each other about all these things that had happened.

01:27.040 --> 01:27.900
While they were talking,

01:27.900 --> 01:31.760
Talking and discussing together, Jesus himself drew near and went with them.

01:32.400 --> 01:34.800
But their eyes were kept from recognizing him.

01:35.340 --> 01:36.300
And he said to them,

01:37.040 --> 01:41.600
What is this conversation that you are holding with each other as you walk?

01:41.920 --> 01:44.180
And they stood still looking sad.

01:44.940 --> 01:47.520
Then one of them, named Cleopas, answered him,

01:47.760 --> 01:53.800
Are you the only visitor to Jerusalem who does not know the things that have happened there in these days?

01:54.140 --> 01:55.520
And he said to them,

01:56.240 --> 01:57.200
What things?

01:57.900 --> 01:59.220
And they said to him,

01:59.920 --> 02:06.800
Concerning Jesus of Nazareth, a man who was a prophet mighty in deed and word before God and all the people,

02:07.260 --> 02:12.920
and how our chief priests and rulers delivered him up to be condemned to death and crucified him.

02:13.600 --> 02:16.820
But we had hoped that he was the one to redeem Israel.

02:17.560 --> 02:22.460
Yes, and besides all this, it is now the third day since these things happened.

02:23.240 --> 02:26.400
Moreover, some women of our company amazed us.

02:26.860 --> 02:27.680
They were at the tomb.

02:27.680 --> 02:31.480
They were at the tomb early in the morning, and when they did not find his body, they came back,

02:31.820 --> 02:35.920
saying that they had even seen a vision of angels who said that he was alive.

02:36.440 --> 02:40.700
Some of those who were with us went to the tomb and found it just as the women had said.

02:41.560 --> 02:43.560
But him they did not see.

02:44.260 --> 02:45.280
And he said to them,

02:46.080 --> 02:51.400
O foolish ones, and slow of heart to believe all that the prophets have spoken.

02:51.920 --> 02:55.980
Was it not necessary that the Christ should suffer these things,

02:56.560 --> 02:57.660
and enter into his kingdom,

02:57.660 --> 02:58.140
and enter into his glory?

02:58.960 --> 03:01.340
And beginning with Moses and all the prophets,

03:01.560 --> 03:05.540
he interpreted to them in all the scriptures the things concerning himself.

03:06.160 --> 03:08.820
So they drew near to the village to which they were going.

03:09.520 --> 03:11.740
He acted as if he were going farther.

03:12.480 --> 03:14.520
But they urged him strongly, saying,

03:15.400 --> 03:20.120
Stay with us, for it is toward evening, and the day is now far spent.

03:20.880 --> 03:22.620
So he went in to stay with them.

03:23.320 --> 03:27.040
When he was at table with them, he took the bread and blessed and broke it,

03:27.040 --> 03:27.640
and gave it to them.

03:27.660 --> 03:31.260
And their eyes were opened, and they recognized him,

03:31.360 --> 03:32.740
and he vanished from their sight.

03:33.520 --> 03:34.820
They said to each other,

03:35.500 --> 03:39.300
Did not our hearts burn within us while he talked to us on the road,

03:39.880 --> 03:42.020
while he opened to us the scriptures?

03:42.840 --> 03:46.120
And they rose that same hour and returned to Jerusalem.

03:46.600 --> 03:50.680
And they found the eleven and those who were with them gathered together, saying,

03:51.200 --> 03:54.780
The Lord has risen indeed, and has appeared to Simon.

03:54.780 --> 03:57.640
Then they told what had happened on the road,

03:57.660 --> 04:00.780
and how he was known to them in the breaking of the bread.

04:01.320 --> 04:03.240
As they were talking about these things,

04:03.740 --> 04:07.080
Jesus himself stood among them, and said to them,

04:07.500 --> 04:08.940
Peace to you.

04:09.580 --> 04:12.720
But they were startled and frightened, and thought they saw a spirit.

04:13.440 --> 04:14.400
And he said to them,

04:15.080 --> 04:16.180
Why are you troubled?

04:16.820 --> 04:19.360
And why do doubts arise in your hearts?

04:20.080 --> 04:24.040
See my hands and my feet, that it is I myself.

04:24.600 --> 04:26.020
Touch me, and see.

04:26.020 --> 04:26.100
See.

04:26.500 --> 04:27.640
For a spirit does not know.

04:27.660 --> 04:30.860
A spirit does not have flesh and bones, as you see that I have.

04:31.520 --> 04:34.900
And when he had said this, he showed them his hands and his feet.

04:35.460 --> 04:39.880
And while they still disbelieved for joy and were marveling, he said to them,

04:40.320 --> 04:42.420
Have you anything here to eat?

04:43.040 --> 04:47.240
They gave him a piece of broiled fish, and he took it and ate before them.

04:47.900 --> 04:48.980
Then he said to them,

04:49.820 --> 04:53.340
These are my words that I spoke to you while I was still with you,

04:53.620 --> 04:57.400
that everything written about me in the law of Moses and the prophets,

04:57.660 --> 04:59.760
and the Psalms must be fulfilled.

05:00.600 --> 05:04.280
Then he opened their minds to understand the Scriptures, and said to them,

05:05.020 --> 05:08.180
Thus it is written, that the Christ should suffer,

05:08.520 --> 05:10.980
and on the third day rise from the dead,

05:11.380 --> 05:15.580
and that repentance and forgiveness of sin should be proclaimed in his name

05:15.580 --> 05:18.820
to all nations, beginning from Jerusalem.

05:19.420 --> 05:21.860
You are witnesses of these things.

05:21.860 --> 05:26.640
And behold, I am sending the promise of my Father upon you.

05:27.220 --> 05:27.640
But still,

05:27.660 --> 05:31.040
stay in the city until you are clothed with power from on high.

05:31.400 --> 05:36.160
Then he led them out as far as Bethany, and lifting up his hands, he blessed them.

05:37.040 --> 05:40.880
While he blessed them, he parted from them and was carried up into heaven.

05:41.600 --> 05:45.500
And they worshipped him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy

05:45.500 --> 05:48.620
and were continually in the temple blessing God.

